      "result": "Implemented the persistent Rails URL shortener with link creation, listing, lookup, redirects, validation, duplicate-code conflicts, and click tracking. `start.sh` is executable; it runs pending migrations and starts the API on `0.0.0.0:8000`. The README explains startup, and the database connection uses `DATABASE_URL`.\n\nVerified the endpoints over HTTP, including malformed JSON, invalid URLs and codes, duplicate codes, redirects and click increments, unknown codes, and the `app` host. PostgreSQL migrations ran successfully.\n\nOne environment compatibility fix: pinned the `json` gem below version 3 so Rails can parse and render JSON requests correctly.",
